\f1\fs22 By the time Gerry Hardman had shoved and elbowed his way down past the emergency foot lighting and out of the darkened Lysander Shakti Memorial Auditorium, an Elvi band was already finishing up their first number on the improvised carpark stage. Among the gear and the flashing lights, Gerry couldn\'92t help but notice the same old geezers\'97the ones Alexander had accused of casting demonic spells\'97standing with ukuleles near the back curtain.\
